!!id:"https://schemas.example.com/2026/40/orders/orders-errors-1.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/core.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/io/ltr8/http/problem.tn"
@doc:"""
  Business errors, each composing `problem.details` and PINNING the status it inherits from it. That fixed
  `status` is how an endpoint's `errors` get an HTTP status without a list of responses: the status is a
  property of the error type, readable from the resolved schema, and a document writing another value is
  a validation error.
  """
!schema {
  sku_not_found   => problem.details & { status: = 404  sku: text }
  order_not_found => problem.details & { status: = 404 }
}
